WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:08.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello there  by the time you're watching this video  i'll probably be somewhere up in the  mountains i guess here  yeah that's me i'm recording this the  night before i leave and my living room  is  a complete mess if by some miracle we  had some big revelations or big nintendo  news the past week  i wouldn't have known about it as of the  time of this recording  keep that in mind so with that said  let's talk about the zonai  now the zone i have become somewhat of a  meme in the zelda community  with some theorists even purposely and  jokingly avoiding mentioning their name  i myself have also consciously avoided  the subject on my channel unless it  involved a collaboration or was used for  comedic purposes  for instance in my breath while 2  trailer breakdown video which is still  the most popular video on my channel i  keep using phrases such as the green  hand  or link's spiritual arm rather than  saying zone eye hand now the biggest  reason i didn't mention them  in that particular video was because i  wanted to keep it as  factual as possible if that's even a  thing  because well we don't have anything else  to work with outside of that trailer  now it's not so much that i don't like  the subject of the zona  in fact it's secretly one of my favorite  mysteries in the entire zelda lore and  the fact that it's a mystery that's  still  completely unsolved and makes it all the  more appealing  nintendo has the tendency to keep things  vague and open to interpretation a lot  of the time but despite if something  isn't necessarily said or  shown in game we can often still create  some very solid theories and if backed  up with enough evidence the zelda  community will accept it as a fact at  some point  as a quick example for instance it's  never stated where  king rome died i think initially most of  us assumed he died  inside the castle when it came under  attack with good reason i mean how do  you even escape  something like this but celtic in one of  his videos presents a very compelling  case for the fact that the king  probably died at the great plateau and  it makes sense if you look at the full  picture  why would his spirit be confined to the  great plateau if he died at the castle  and celtic also proves with pretty much  100  certainty that the pile of rocks we see  on the top of mount hylia is the king's  grave in a case like this  we have enough to work with and enough  evidence that points into a certain  direction but with the zonai  we don't have that even with creating a  champion in mind  it's still very much up in the air they  mentioned just enough to spark our  curiosity but not enough to create a  solid theory about  we've seen plenty of mysterious races in  the zelda series  like the oku from twilight princess a  very mysterious race who live high up in  the sky and are said to be the closest  to the gods and although we don't know  that much about them we at least know  what they look  like to our dismay same goes for the  wind tribe from minish cap or the  twilight but the zonai  no idea we have no idea what they even  looked like we don't know when they  lived  what their role was who they were loyal  to or allied with  and that is exactly what makes  theorizing about them such a  double-edged sword  on one hand we want to solve this puzzle  on the other hand we don't really have  enough to work with  and if nintendo had left it at that and  just moved on to a completely new  zelda game in a new era it would have  probably stayed that way  but then we got that glorious e3 trailer  of breathaly 2 last year  and what did it show zonai architecture  it's all over the place  now i don't want to speak for other  people too much but i don't think most  theorists necessarily think the zonai  are going to be the biggest thing in  zelda history ever like it's gonna  reveal like the meaning of life behind  the whole zelda universe or something  like that but we're at least hoping that  this game  will give us that missing piece of the  puzzle so we can build a solid theory  about them  and then we can just check them off the  list and categorize them just like we  did with the other mysterious tribes in  the zelda series  it's why many people are so passionate  about zelda lore we love playing  detective and solving mysteries  it's also why the zelda theorist  community is so close and you can always  see people doing collaborations with  each other and expanding upon each  other's theories  zelda lore is a puzzle too big for one  person to solve the subject of the zonai  is simply one of the most recent  mysteries that we want to get the  answers to  and when looking at the trailer there's  at least a strong case to be made that  we will  probably see something related to them  so that pretty much covers  why zelda theorists are so obsessed with  this tribe as of late but what about the  other people  you know the haters i'm of course not  being serious but there are a lot of  people who are sick and tired of hearing  about them  and i think the two biggest reasons for  this is  one too many strong assumptions with too  little evidence  and two an over saturation of the market  aka  too much content about them and yeah i  can see that point of view  i mean we did get a lot of zonai related  subjects in just one year  obviously for the reasons i talked about  earlier as a theorist it's sometimes  very easy to forget that a large  large majority of players probably  didn't even think anything about the  zona when they first discovered their  ruins  i know i didn't when i first played the  game in my eyes it was just  another ancient ruin i mean we saw  plenty of those across the whole map  right and had it not been for creating a  champion and then subsequently the  release of the breath the wall 2 trailer  i probably would have still thought the  same way about it just another  ancient ruin of people who have been in  gone nothing to see here folks  because when you think about it the  zonai are never mentioned in game  no npc dialogue no scriptures nothing  all we have is the name of the location  itself the closest we get to any in-game  information is the barbarian armor set  but even that one doesn't state their  name  it just says it belonged to a savage  tribe who lived in faron  hence why i can totally understand why  some people are like why are these  people  all talking about this zona tribe all of  a sudden now i'm a very positive person  and i don't get very angry at stuff  especially if it's fiction  but i can't understand that some people  might be annoyed with the way a theory  is presented there's a pretty big  difference between  harmless theory crafting and stuff like  that and making it sound like you have  the answers you've got it all figured  out which  let's be fair here nobody does at least  not about this subject  all we have is best guesses it's why i  very much appreciate the zonai video  nintendo black crisis did  it mostly sticks to the facts the stuff  we already know  it's a compilation almost it doesn't  force an entire narrative upon you  which a lot of theories tend to do but i  don't feel like that's on purpose  people just enjoy making a good story  about it and well  sharing it with the rest of us now like  i said i personally  love the zonai subject i eat that stuff  up i love watching content and theories  about  them i like all the creative stories  everybody has come up with  but at the same time in the back of my  mind i do realize that of course  probably 99 of all that stuff is not  correct but hey that doesn't make it  less fun to watch  at this point there are so many  completely different theories out there  i'm actually kind of curious to see who  got it right in the end  it's almost like a lottery and yeah like  i said there has been a huge influx of  zonai theories ever since the e3 trailer  so i get why some people are very tired  of the subject but at the same time it's  also important to understand that this  trailer is  all we have to work with and what it  shows isn't much  so there's only so much we can cover  about it and it seems like there's still  a very significant audience out there  who love seeing people talk about breath  the while too  and since nintendo doesn't seem to give  us any information anytime soon we  try to keep the hype alive i guess let  me know down in the comments what you  guys  think whatever idea you have about it or  about the subject  people talking about it too much too  little i don't know  just share your opinions or theories  because i always love reading them  so with that said i gotta go now it's  getting late and tomorrow i have 10  hours of sitting behind the wheel in  front of me so i gotta get some sleep  i will be back soon and until then this  is dawn signing off and  have a good one

